ONE-MINUTE INTERVIEW ANSWER
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Q: Does Java support operator overloading?

A:

"Java does not support user-defined operator overloading.
This keeps the language simple, readable, and avoids ambiguity.

However, Java has predefined operator behavior. For example,
the `+` operator performs numeric addition and can also concatenate
Strings."


