Q62. RUNTIME POLYMORPHISM
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Definition:

Runtime polymorphism occurs when a parent reference refers to a
child object and an overridden method is selected at runtime.

Example:

class Animal {

    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal");
    }
}

class Cat extends Animal {

    @Override
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Cat");
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Animal a = new Cat();

        a.sound();
    }
}


Output:

Cat


How it works:

Animal a = new Cat();
       ↑        ↑
 Reference    Object
  Type        Type


a.sound();

        ↓

Actual object = Cat

        ↓

Cat.sound() executes


Important Terms:

Parent reference
      +
Child object
      +
Method overriding
      ↓
Runtime Polymorphism


Interview Answer:

> Runtime polymorphism is achieved through method overriding,
> where a parent class reference refers to a child class object
> and the overridden method is resolved at runtime.


