Q63. ENCAPSULATION USING GETTERS AND SETTERS
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Definition:

Encapsulation means bundling data and methods together while
restricting direct access to internal data.

Example:

class Animal {

    private String name;

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Animal a = new Animal();

        a.setName("Cat");

        System.out.println(a.getName());
    }
}


Output:

Cat


Working:

private String name;
        ↓
Direct access restricted
        ↓
setName()
        ↓
Modify data

getName()
        ↓
Access data


Important:

Getter → retrieves/returns data

Setter → modifies/updates data


Interview Trap:

Getter and setter alone do not define encapsulation.

The main idea is:

> Bundling data and methods together while restricting direct
> access to the internal data.


