Q66. WHAT IS THE JAVA COLLECTIONS FRAMEWORK?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

The Java Collections Framework is a unified architecture of
interfaces, classes, and algorithms used to store and manipulate
groups of objects efficiently.

It provides data structures such as:

• List
• Set
• Queue
• Map

Common implementations:

• ArrayList
• LinkedList
• HashSet
• TreeSet
• HashMap
• TreeMap


Important:

Collections Framework does NOT simply "reduce time complexity".

Different implementations provide different performance
characteristics for different operations.


