Q71. ARRAY vs ARRAYLIST
----------------------------------------------------------------------

+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------+
| Feature          | Array                   | ArrayList             |
+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------+
| Size             | Fixed                   | Dynamic               |
| Index access     | Yes                     | Yes                   |
| Duplicates       | Yes                     | Yes                   |
| Primitive types  | Yes                     | No, uses wrappers     |
| add/remove APIs  | No collection APIs      | Yes                   |
| Random access     | O(1)                    | O(1)                  |
+------------------+-------------------------+----------------------+

Array:

int[] arr = new int[5];

Size is fixed after creation.


ArrayList:

ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();

list.add(10);
list.add(20);
list.add(30);


