Q82. HASHMAP vs CONCURRENTHASHMAP
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

HashMap is not thread-safe, whereas ConcurrentHashMap is designed
for concurrent access by multiple threads.

ConcurrentHashMap provides thread-safe operations while allowing
better concurrency than synchronizing an entire map.


+-------------------+----------------------+----------------------+
| Feature           | HashMap              | ConcurrentHashMap    |
+-------------------+----------------------+----------------------+
| Thread-safe       | No                   | Yes                  |
| Concurrent access | Not designed for it  | Designed for it      |
| Null key          | One allowed          | Not allowed          |
| Null values       | Allowed              | Not allowed          |
| Main use          | Normal applications  | Multithreaded apps   |
+-------------------+----------------------+----------------------+


Memory Trick:

HashMap
→ Normal
→ Not thread-safe
→ Allows null


ConcurrentHashMap
→ Concurrent
→ Thread-safe
→ No null keys/values


Why not simply synchronize HashMap?

Synchronizing an entire map can serialize access and reduce
concurrency.

ConcurrentHashMap is specifically designed for concurrent access
