Q88. WHAT IS COMPARABLE?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

Comparable is an interface in Java used to define the natural
ordering of objects.

A class implements Comparable and overrides the compareTo() method
to define how its objects should be compared and sorted.

Syntax:

class Student implements Comparable<Student> {

    @Override
    public int compareTo(Student other) {
