    String[] words = str.split("\\s+");

    for (String word : words) {
        map.put(word, map.getOrDefault(word, 0) + 1);
    }

    return map;
}


Example:

Input:

"java is easy java is powerful"


Output:

java     → 2
is       → 2
easy     → 1
powerful → 1


Flow:

Sentence
    ↓
split("\\s+")
    ↓
String[]
    ↓
HashMap
    ↓
word → frequency


IMPORTANT:

split("\\s+")

is preferable to:

split(" ")


because \\s+ handles one or more whitespace characters.


Complexity:

Time  → O(n)
Space → O(k)

n = number of words
k = number of distinct words


