Q128. HOW DO YOU READ DATA FROM A FILE?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

In Java, we can read data from a file using classes and methods
provided by java.io and java.nio.file.

For example, Files.readString() can read the complete content of a
text file, while BufferedReader can read text line by line.


Using Files.readString():

import java.nio.file.*;

String data = Files.readString(Path.of("data.txt"));

System.out.println(data);


Using BufferedReader:

BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(
    new FileReader("data.txt")
);

String line;

while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
    System.out.println(line);
}

br.close();


Common APIs:

java.io
    → FileReader
    → BufferedReader

java.nio.file
    → Files.readString()
    → Files.readAllLines()


Interview Trap:

❌ "Java has a read method for file handling."

✅ Mention the specific API/class and method being used.


