Q131. WHAT IS MULTITHREADING?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

Multithreading is a Java feature that allows multiple threads to
execute concurrently within a process.

Threads share common resources such as Heap memory, but each thread
has its own Stack and execution state.

Example:

                Java Process
                     |
          +----------+----------+
          |                     |
       Thread 1              Thread 2
          |                     |
      Own Stack              Own Stack
          |                     |
          +----------+----------+
                     |
              Shared Heap
              Shared Resources


Important:

Threads
→ Share Heap
→ Have their own Stack
→ Can execute concurrently


Concurrency vs Parallelism:

Single CPU Core
→ Context switching
→ Concurrency

Multiple CPU Cores
→ Threads can execute simultaneously
→ Parallelism


Memory:

THREADS
→ Share Heap
→ Own Stack
→ Execute Concurrently


======================================================================
Q132. WHY DO WE USE MULTITHREADING?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Interview Answer:

We use multithreading to improve application responsiveness,
CPU utilization, and performance by allowing multiple tasks to
execute concurrently.

Benefits:

• Better responsiveness
• Better CPU utilization
• Concurrent execution
• Parallel execution on multiple cores
• Useful for independent tasks


Example:

Without multithreading:

Task A → Complete
          ↓
Task B → Complete
          ↓
Task C → Complete


With multithreading:

Thread 1 → Task A
Thread 2 → Task B
Thread 3 → Task C

        ↓
Concurrent execution


Important:

On a single CPU core:

→ Threads share CPU time using context switching.

On multiple CPU cores:

→ Threads can actually execute in parallel.


Memory:

Single Core
→ Context Switching
→ Concurrency

Multiple Cores
→ True Parallelism


